Kickstarting AgentVault's First 50 Users
1. Target User Segments
A. Young Crypto Traders (18–25)
If I had to choose the first group to target, I would start with young crypto traders.
The reason is that they are already active in online crypto communities and are usually open to trying new tools. Many of them spend time on Twitter, Discord, Telegram, and Reddit to learn about new projects and trading opportunities.
One challenge I often see is that new traders rely heavily on social media trends, influencers, or market hype. As a result, they can struggle to identify useful information and make informed decisions.
AgentVault can help by providing faster insights and making research easier, allowing users to spend less time searching for information and more time making decisions.
Where I would find them:
Twitter/X
Discord crypto communities
Telegram groups
Reddit crypto forums
College blockchain and Web3 clubs
B. Active Crypto Traders
My second target group would be active traders who participate in the market regularly.
I chose them because they already understand the value of good information and are always looking for ways to improve their trading process. Since they follow the market closely, they can quickly tell whether a product is useful.
Their biggest challenge is keeping track of market news, token updates, and trading opportunities across multiple platforms.
AgentVault can act as a research assistant that helps them analyze information faster and stay updated without spending hours gathering data manually.
Where I would find them:
TradingView communities
Binance and Bybit communities
Crypto Discord servers
Telegram trading channels
Twitter/X trading communities
