3. GTM Ideas
Idea 1: College Blockchain Club Outreach
I would reach out to blockchain and Web3 clubs in colleges and offer members early access to AgentVault in exchange for feedback. Students are often interested in crypto and AI tools, making them a good source of early adopters. This can help build an engaged user base at a very low cost.
Idea 2: Discord Community Outreach
Instead of spending money on ads initially, I would participate in crypto Discord communities, understand the discussions happening there, and introduce AgentVault to interested users. Building trust first would make users more likely to try the product and provide honest feedback.
Idea 3: Crypto Meme Contest
Crypto communities are highly active on memes and social engagement. I would launch a simple meme contest on Twitter/X and Discord where users create memes related to crypto trading, market trends, or AI in crypto.
Participants would join the AgentVault community and share their memes using a specific hashtag. Winners could receive early access to new features, exclusive beta access, or recognition within the community.
This would help increase awareness, encourage user-generated content, and attract new users organically without requiring a large marketing budget.
Conclusion
For the first 50 users, I would focus mainly on young crypto traders and active traders. Young traders are easier to reach and more willing to test new products, while active traders can provide valuable feedback that helps improve the product. Together, these two groups can provide the initial user base and feedback needed to improve AgentVault before expanding to a larger audience.

